---
description: Prefer production efficiency and correctness over simplistic shortcuts
alwaysApply: true
---

docforge-quality:

- Optimize for production efficiency, correctness, observability, and replaceable providers — not toy/simple stubs when a durable approach exists.
- Prefer bounded concurrency (worker pools / errgroup + semaphores) for page-level work.
- Prefer real parsers/libraries for PDF detect/extract when available (CPU-only, ARM64 + x86_64).
- Keep stages idempotent: reuse existing stage artifacts before rerunning expensive work.
- Providers stay isolated and must not write job/DB state; orchestrator owns workflow transitions.
- Exporters consume CDOM only.
- Add/update tests for new behavior, including failure and cancel paths.
- Do not sacrifice API/CDOM/domain contract stability for speed.
